 "text": "Hello, how are things going? Keep it well wrapped in a cooler with ice. If the ice runs out, get more right away. Ice cubes melt fast. A block of ice that lasts several days is worth a spot in most coolers. Keep the cooler shut and out of direct sun. An open cooler can freeze dry everything inside. He' stop if you ask nicely. A cold weekend cooler is worth fighting for. Yes, each time you put cold ice in, pour out any meltwater and wipe inside with a wet towel. This keeps the cooler from getting warm spots.",
